{"uid":"modules/lazy_verify.py","name":"lazy_verify.py","qualname":"modules/lazy_verify.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/lazy_verify.py","line":1,"end_line":260,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Structured read-only verification of loop findings.","description":"Replaces the old substring-grep retest verdicts with a small fixed set\nof read-only checks whose verdict rules are deterministic:\n\n  http_probe   one HEAD (GET only when the server answers 405 to HEAD),\n               no cookies, no credentials, no redirects, body discarded\n  tcp_probe    one socket connect against the single named port\n  banner_probe one connect that reads a banner and matches it against\n               the finding's needle\n  nmap_sv      ``nmap -sV`` against the single port the finding names\n               (only when the nmap binary exists)\n\nVerdict rules, faithful to the reference discipline:\n\n- a check that reproduces the finding marks the finding **reproduced**;\n- a check that did not reproduce it NEVER proves it fixed (a template\n  can miss: a WAF, a virtual host, a different path) — the verdict\n  stays inconclusive and a retry is scheduled;\n- every check records exactly the command it ran and a capped evidence\n  snippet, so the finding carries what actually happened.\n\nStdlib only; every check is bounded and non-fatal.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/lazy_verify.py::CHECK_KINDS","modules/lazy_verify.py::EVIDENCE_CAP","modules/lazy_verify.py::plan_checks","modules/lazy_verify.py::run_check","modules/lazy_verify.py::verdict_from_checks","modules/lazy_verify.py::verify_finding"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
